   "id": 40,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2740,
    80
   ],
   "size": [
    380,
    600
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 45,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "HOW TO READ THIS DEBUG WORKFLOW\n\n1. Set the INPUT folder (PNG frames of your plate, e.g. the _render folder the Nuke panel writes), start_index and cap (few frames = fast).\n2. Queue. Then read the previews in order:\n\u2460 who is detected as a person\n\u2461 where the crops are (body = green, head = amber)\n\u2462 what Sapiens sees in each crop and the normals it returns\n\u2463 all crops pasted back\n\u2464 where Sapiens is used (white) vs MoGe (black)\n\u2465 MoGe normals\n\u2466 merge before stabilization\n\u2467 final N\n\u2469 the plate as LTX sees it (fitted to 1920, padded)\n\u246a the LTX Alpha Gen matte written to A\n\nCHECK A must be black on the people: the merged normals there are exactly the crop normals.\nCHECK B shows only what the RAFT stabilization changed.\nThe numbers (mean / 95%) are written on the heatmaps and in the console.\n\nEXRs go to ComfyUI/output/debug/ (not your Nuke passes).\nEvery preview is also saved as PNG in ComfyUI/output/nukebridge_debug/<RUN TAG>/ (or the folder you set)."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
